# Admitted knowledge. Every asset body is covered by its `content_hash` (D19,
# D35) and every asset.yaml carries that hash, so reformatting either breaks the
# integrity check the build performs -- and, worse, silently stops the body from
# being byte-identical to the section it was imported from at a pinned revision.
# Prettier did exactly that once: it rewrote quote style and blank lines in
# thirteen imported bodies, and `pnpm build:index` refused the whole tree.
